CineComic - Privacy Policy

Effective date: September 29, 2026

CineComic ("the app") is made by Some Foolish App. This policy explains what
happens to your information when you use the app. The short version: the app
does not collect, store on any server, share or sell any personal data, and it
contains no ads and no analytics.


1. Information we collect

None. CineComic does not collect personal information of any kind. It has no
user accounts, no sign-in, no advertising, no analytics and no crash-reporting
services, and it does not ask for your name, email address, location, contacts
or any other personal details.

The app does not request internet access, so it cannot send anything from your
device to us or to anyone else.


2. Your comics

CineComic opens the comic files (CBZ and CBR) that you choose, from the folder
you pick or a file you open with the app. Your comics are read directly on your
device and are never uploaded or copied anywhere else.

Finding the panels and speech balloons on each page is done entirely on your
device, using models built into the app. No page, image or text ever leaves your
device.


3. Information kept on your device

So that the app works the way you expect, it keeps some information locally, in
the app's own storage on your device:

  - where you are in each comic, and the comics you have opened recently;
  - your reading-time statistics, such as time read today and comics completed;
  - your settings, and which way each of your folders reads;
  - small cover images for the comics in your library.

This information stays on your device. We never receive it and cannot see it.
You can delete it at any time by clearing the app's data in your device's
settings or by uninstalling the app.


4. Device backups

Android can include apps' settings in the backups it makes to your Google
account, if you have turned on backup in your device's settings. If you have,
the information described in section 3 may be part of that backup. Backups are
made and stored by Google under your own account and your device's settings;
Some Foolish App has no access to them. You can turn backup off in your
device's settings.


5. Permissions

CineComic uses access to your files only to read the comics you choose to open.
It does not read, change or send any other files.


6. Purchases

If you buy CineComic on Google Play, the purchase is handled entirely by Google
under Google's own privacy policy. We do not receive your payment details.


7. Children

CineComic is not directed at children under 13 and does not knowingly collect
information from anyone, including children.


8. Changes to this policy

If this policy changes, the new version will be posted at the same address with
a new effective date.


